  "narrative": "The causal analysis using LinearDML estimates an average treatment effect (ATE) of 0.03 (95% CI: [0.02, 0.05]). This effect is classified as small and is statistically significant. The effect passed 4 out of 5 robustness tests, indicating the finding is likely genuine and not spurious. Robust to confounding at measured strength. Explaining this effect away would need an unmeasured confounder with a risk ratio of at least 1.26 with both treatment and outcome (1.18 at the CI bound), stronger than all measured confounding combined (1.03, the confounding the adjustment removed, naive vs adjusted). Because this effect is significant and cleared the robustness gate, the practical next step is to act on treatment dupixent \u2014 focus on increasing it for the segment where it is currently lowest \u2014 and confirm the lift in persistent at 180d g28 against a matched holdout before scaling.",
